// Mirage Bowl (docs/LAYOUTS.md; the LA direction in docs/SCENARIOS.md, "Mirage Bowl 2001"):
// a city made to be seen from a car, in a bowl you can always see the rim of. A flat floor of
// one-story sheds and bungalows, a long mountain front across the north with one high summit
// that the main avenue drives straight at, lower ranges east and west, rail yards to the
// south. Strip corridors run along the boulevards; an old road cuts across the grid on a
// diagonal toward the summit; a few towers stand downtown against the mountains; a lone
// knoll in the flats and a spur of the front range carry lookouts over the lights.
//
// Meters, x east, z south, (0, 0) the north-west corner; 24 x 24 chunks, 3072 m square.
